## Procedure
1. Reproduce: run the failing command yourself (shown above) and read the real output.
2. Find the root cause. Say it in one sentence before you edit anything.
3. Make the smallest change that fixes the cause. Fix the CODE so it meets the spec. If you add a dependency to a manifest, run `./scripts/sdlc sync`.
4. Re-run just the failing gate: `./scripts/sdlc gates --only <gate-id>`; then the whole `./scripts/sdlc verify`.

## Hard rules (the loop enforces some of these and stops with an integrity violation)
- DO NOT edit `.ai/sdlc.json`, `scripts/sdlc*`, `.github/workflows/`, or anything under `.ai/specs/` (PRDs and acceptance checks). Healing fixes code, not the definition of correct.
- DO NOT delete, skip (`xfail`, `.skip`, `-k` filters) or weaken tests, lower coverage thresholds, add `# noqa` / `eslint-disable` / `type: ignore` to silence a real problem, or mock the thing under test.
- DO NOT regenerate `.ai/contract/openapi.json` just to make the contract gate pass. It changes only when the PRD intentionally changes the API.
- If you believe the spec itself is wrong, STOP and say so in your final message instead of changing it.

